<% content_for :title, "Error Handling" %>

<div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Error Handling</h1>
  <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 mb-8">
    Understanding API errors and how to handle them in your application.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Error Response Format</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    All API errors return a consistent JSON format:
  </p>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "error": "Error message describing what went wrong",
  "code": "ERROR_CODE",
  "details": {}  // Optional additional context
}</pre>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">HTTP Status Codes</h2>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <table class="w-full text-sm mb-8">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/30">
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Code</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Meaning</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">200</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">OK</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Request succeeded</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">201</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Created</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Resource created successfully</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">400</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Bad Request</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Invalid request parameters</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-red-500/15 text-red-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">401</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Unauthorized</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Missing or invalid API key</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-red-500/15 text-red-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">403</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Forbidden</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Valid key but insufficient permissions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">404</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Not Found</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Resource not found</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">422</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Unprocessable Entity</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Validation errors</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-red-500/15 text-red-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">429</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Too Many Requests</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Rate limit exceeded</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="px-2 py-1 bg-red-500/15 text-red-500 rounded font-mono text-xs">500</span></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Internal Server Error</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Something went wrong on our end</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Common Errors</h2>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100 mt-6 mb-3">Authentication Errors (401)</h3>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "error": "Invalid or missing API key",
  "code": "INVALID_API_KEY"
}</pre>
  </div>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    <strong class="text-slate-100">How to fix:</strong> Ensure your API key is included in the request header and is valid.
    Check that you're using either <code class="bg-pd-tertiary px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm">Authorization: Bearer pdat_...</code>
    or <code class="bg-pd-tertiary px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm">X-API-Key: pdat_...</code>.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100 mt-6 mb-3">Validation Errors (422)</h3>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "error": "Validation failed",
  "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
  "details": {
    "domain": ["is required", "must be a valid domain"]
  }
}</pre>
  </div>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    <strong class="text-slate-100">How to fix:</strong> Check the <code class="bg-pd-tertiary px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm">details</code>
    object for specific field errors and correct your request.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100 mt-6 mb-3">Rate Limit Errors (429)</h3>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "error": "Rate limit exceeded",
  "code": "RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED",
  "details": {
    "retry_after": 60,
    "limit": 100,
    "remaining": 0,
    "reset_at": "2024-01-15T10:31:00Z"
  }
}</pre>
  </div>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    <strong class="text-slate-100">How to fix:</strong> Wait for the <code class="bg-pd-tertiary px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm">retry_after</code>
    period before making more requests. Consider using bulk endpoints to reduce the number of requests.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Best Practices</h2>

  <ul class="text-slate-300 space-y-3 mb-8">
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Always check the status code</strong> — Don't assume success; check for 2xx status codes</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Parse error responses</strong> — Use the error message and code to provide meaningful feedback</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Implement retry logic</strong> — For 429 and 5xx errors, implement exponential backoff</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Log errors</strong> — Keep track of errors for debugging and monitoring</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Example Error Handling</h2>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100 mt-6 mb-3">JavaScript</h3>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">async function checkDomain(domain) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(
      'https://phish.directory/api/v1/domain/check',
      {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Authorization': 'Bearer pdat_your_api_key',
          'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({ domain })
      }
    );

    if (!response.ok) {
      const error = await response.json();

      switch (response.status) {
        case 401:
          throw new Error('Invalid API key');
        case 429:
          const retryAfter = error.details?.retry_after || 60;
          throw new Error(`Rate limited. Retry in ${retryAfter}s`);
        default:
          throw new Error(error.error || 'Unknown error');
      }
    }

    return await response.json();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('API Error:', error.message);
    throw error;
  }
}</pre>
  </div>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100 mt-6 mb-3">Python</h3>
  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">import requests
import time

def check_domain(domain, max_retries=3):
    headers = {'Authorization': 'Bearer pdat_your_api_key'}

    for attempt in range(max_retries):
        response = requests.post(
            'https://phish.directory/api/v1/domain/check',
            headers=headers,
            json={'domain': domain}
        )

        if response.status_code == 200:
            return response.json()

        if response.status_code == 429:
            retry_after = response.json().get('details', {}).get('retry_after', 60)
            time.sleep(retry_after)
            continue

        error = response.json()
        raise Exception(f"API Error: {error.get('error')}")

    raise Exception("Max retries exceeded")</pre>
  </div>
</div>
